Unravel ESP32 Rust integration

The AgentLoop, Session, model, tools, events, cancellation, and error
implementations in vendor/unravel-agent-runtime/src originate from
https://github.com/unravelaidk/unravel-agent-runtime at revision
c507d6b2b2514527a572b0d2331aef34961ba652 (crates/unravel-agent-runtime/src).
They are locally modified, not an unchanged upstream copy.

Local ESP32 integration changes (2026-10-14) include:
- A standalone dependency manifest avoiding desktop Tokio features.
- Actual provider call IDs and conversation/provider-session/run/generation
  identity in the tool execution context, with deadline and cancellation.
- Explicit succeeded/failed/unknown/cancelled/partial tool result states and
  propagation of uncertain outcomes into the existing orchestration lifecycle.
- A synchronous checkpoint hook before requests and between public turn
  iterations, used by the embedded bridge for archive acknowledgment and
  bounded complete-tool-group context compaction.

The upstream authors' attribution, source revision, AGPL-3.0-only license,
and the earlier ServoLoop/Khadim provenance remain in the vendored NOTICE.

The C ABI and callback-backed OpenAI adapter in this directory are integration
code, distributed under AGPL-3.0-only. See vendor/unravel-agent-runtime/LICENSE
and vendor/unravel-agent-runtime/NOTICE for license text and upstream attribution.
